    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d167">

                <pb facs="0287" n="1041" xml:id="pg1041"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 658.119/14</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Sweden</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-08-27T14:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 27, 1917, 2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received August 28, 12.40
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>682. On the 23d instant Swedish Minister for Foreign Affairs delivered a public
                    address in Stockholm in the course of which he said that the Swedish Government
                    would not sever commercial relations with the Central powers as a condition to
                    obtaining foodstuffs from America. He stated that the population of Sweden need
                    not fear a famine during the coming year and that the Government therefore will
                    not be compelled to accept an agreement which is unacceptable to the Swedish
                    people. The Minister for Foreign Affairs added, however, that the Government
                    will endeavor to come to an agreement with the United States. A copy of the
                    address is being forwarded to the Department by mail.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d167-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
